review:
For TW:WH1 and WH2 players you certainly don't want to miss out on the qol improvements in this game. The new campaign feels better than the old vortex campaign in WH2. It adds some awesome new factions and units and more freedom in unit control. 

If you are new however, you still cant go wrong with warhammer 2. And it might be better to buy wh2 and wh1 in a sale to build up your assets first, let me explain;

In the WH games the meat of the game lies in the grand campaign called Mortal Empires, which is present in 1,2 and 3 by default. With every new warhammer game you get some extra playable factions and minor qol/graphics improvements. So you could say that from WH1 onwards, every sequel acts as a big DLC pack. More than 50% of the factions/units is unlocked by owning just warhammer 1 and 2 without even their DLC factions. You can buy those 2 games on a sale (+ plus the DLC factions that you really want to try out soon) for a turd and try the franchise out. If you enjoyed the experience you buy WH:3 later when the price is lower.

TLDR;

Yes you can buy WH3 as a standalone game but you might want to build up WH1 and 2 portfolio first.

FOR SIGMAR!!!

{Edit: Too many bugs. For the price of DLCs they launch (even twice every year is frankly unachievable for them now), there isn't the clean gaming experience you expect.

Thumbs down. Sir, Mr. Witch Hunter here are your heretics.}

